    "interpretation": [
        "Local synthetic viewers of one match; sequential 180-second phases with a halfway reconnect. Not registered-user counts or production capacity.",
        "The API, worker and generator share the host. Dedicated live-read and SSE pools are benchmark configuration only.",
        "100 viewers met live-read and publication-to-receipt p95 budgets but missed one write slot.",
        "1000 viewers failed latency and reliability budgets.",
        "10000 viewers is an overload experiment, not a valid capacity latency measurement: generator p95 lag 897.04 ms, maximum 25982.99 ms; 8976 stale viewers.",
        "Granian 2.8.2 defaults to backlog 1024 and per-worker backpressure backlog/workers. The two-worker SSE pool therefore admits about 1024 concurrent requests in this configuration; the 10000 phase recorded only 2048 ready connections across both connection waves.",
        "Publication-to-receipt excludes transaction and snapshot preparation. Successful-request latency percentiles exclude failed requests; use outcome and error counters alongside them.",
        "Backend runtime matched the recorded HEAD; its uncommitted backend diff only changed integration tests. The scoreboard fix is covered by separate component and Chromium/WebKit tests."
    ],
